figs/**/*
!figs/**/.gitkeep
data/*_processing.pickle
data/MM_*.pickle
# data/*.nwb: fully regenerable pipeline output (pipeline/processing.py +
# pipeline/analysis.py from raw NAS data), not source -- tracking every
# re-run in git permanently bloats history (HDF5/NWB binaries don't delta-
# compress between versions). Untracked deliberately; disseminated via a
# GitHub Release when ready rather than committed directly. Same reasoning
# for all_fourier_df.parquet -- it's derived entirely from data/*.nwb +
# data/precomputed/*.pickle via pipeline/aggregate.py, so keeping it
# tracked while its inputs aren't would be inconsistent.
data/*.nwb
data/manuscript/all_fourier_df.parquet
# data/fig1_raw/: raw-voltage snippets for Fig1's exemplar-unit panels,
# extracted from NAS by pipeline/manuscript/fig1_extract_raw_snippets.py --
# same "not source, regenerable, disseminate via Release" reasoning as the
# .nwb files above.
data/fig1_raw/
logs/
*.xlsx
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb
*.egg-info/
.claude/
pipeline/manuscript/64c94b448ce6028c013b0143/
